          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Women in Science</strong><br>\nCori's success served as an inspiration for women in the sciences, proving that they could achieve at the highest levels of research and scientific discovery. Her perseverance in the face of discrimination paved the way for future generations of women scientists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Honors and Recognition</strong><br>\nIn addition to the Nobel Prize, Cori received numerous other honors, including the Garvan-Olin Medal and induction into the National Women's Hall of Fame. Her pioneering spirit was recognized by scientific communities and the public alike.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Remembering Gerty Cori</strong><br>\nGerty Cori passed away in 1957, but her legacy is carried on by the many scientists and students she influenced. She remains a role model for aspiring female scientists and her discoveries continue to be a fundamental part of scientific and medical education.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
